tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Scrape/build tooling is kept local, not published.
/scripts/

# So is everything it reads and writes: the scraped wiki pages, any guides,
# the hand-curated overrides and source screenshots. None of it is needed to
# build the site, which consumes only src/data/*.json.
# (Anchored to the root on purpose: an unanchored "data/" also matches
# src/data/, which holds the two files the app actually reads.)
/data/

# The handoff and decision record stay local too, like the tooling they
# describe; the public README is deliberately kept shallow.
/CLAUDE.md
/STATUS.md
